# Line endings are pinned to LF because this project claims a reproducible build.
#
# solc hashes the *source text* into the CBOR metadata it appends to the runtime
# bytecode (foundry.toml sets bytecode_hash = "ipfs"). Git on Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, so without this file the same commit checks out as CRLF on a
# Windows clone and LF on a Linux one — the same source, different bytes, a different
# metadata hash, and therefore a different bytecode tail. That would break A-12's
# byte-identical claim across machines and can downgrade explorer verification from a
# full match to a partial one.
#
# The blobs are already stored as LF, so this changes no committed content. It only
# stops the working tree from drifting per platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Assets must be delivered byte-for-byte; never run them through text conversion.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.svg text eol=lf
